    "summary": "Review of the second-scenario direct check f8caf123581f4c9abfa7d55569cfcfbe for unit-claim-heartbeat-header-gate, preflight-validated with valid=True and no diagnostics.\n\nFresh execution 7628b537f51c4a868e8ebb80cf019fc2 completed the comparison: the declarative prerequisite matched, comparison_complete and witness_complete are true, and the implication held as expected. After an out-of-window pure heartbeat the receiver adopted the sender as its known leader (ghost_leader_adopted true, known_leader_id ghost) and rejected an otherwise acceptable vote request from the configured candidate node2 (legitimate_vote_granted false), while the same request on a node that never saw the heartbeat was granted (true). That is the downstream availability consequence of the skipped RPC-header gate, corroborating the confirmed violation rather than adding a new one.\n\nProduct contents: the required checker_correspondence item (no_issue_found, empty counterevidence) covering requirement versus predicate, caller duties, identity/correlation, the event-based oracle, completion, and limits; an applicability item; and a re-resolution of the claim-level applicability issue c5b1dc9500994c069cfd0362d39da853 (the processHeartbeat main-thread comment versus the transport's connection-goroutine usage), which is open again for this artifact because a resolution answers its own lineage — disposed as independent_scope with sources.\n\nExplicitly retained: the heartbeat was delivered by invoking the handler body directly, with the transport classification a sourced premise (InmemTransport does not implement the fast path); reachability of an out-of-window peer in a legal deployment is assumed rather than established; no timing, live cluster or election was exercised, so only the receiver's state-dependent decision is shown; and the threading question remains an open concurrency limit for a separate obligation.\n\nRun state: four confirmed in-scope violations, with both the heartbeat and TimeoutNow findings now also carrying measured consequence evidence; no pending review work beyond this product."
